{"source":"Quaggles/dcs-lua-datamine commit fe1d800 (DCS 2.9.29.27278)","dcsVersion":"2.9.29.27278","note":"IR (heat) data read from DCS's own Lua (Quaggles/dcs-lua-datamine, DCS 2.9.29.27278). aspect: prbCoeff k7 = 0.5, the factor on a jet's IR value by the side a seeker sees (front k7, beam 1, rear 2 - k7). fov: full instantaneous IR seeker field of view, degrees (ED comment 'IR GOS + - 1 degree'; the seeker blocks' FOV = 0.0349 rad). planes: DCS type -> [IR_emission_coeff, IR_emission_coeff_ab], a unitless IR value where 1.0 = a Su-27 without afterburner; the second value (afterburner) is null when DCS gives 0 or none (no afterburner); 144 planes and 26 helicopters. planeSrc: DCS type -> the file:line of its IR_emission_coeff in the datamine (_G/...). missiles: every IR-seeker missile (rockets/*.lua with Head_Type 1, plus RIM_116A, which has an IR_seeker block). display = display_name; ssd = SeekerSensivityDistance, m (the seeker's reach against a target of IR value 1); ccm = ccm_k0, flare susceptibility (0 = immune, 1 = medium, higher = easier to decoy); gen = SeekerGen (null when DCS gives none); cooled = SeekerCooled; angles in degrees: offBoresight = Fi_start (look angle at launch), gimbal = Fi_excort (seeker gimbal limit), aspectLimit = Fi_rak (allowed target aspect off its tail: 180 = all-aspect), search = Fi_search (search/scan angle); trackRate = OmViz_max, deg/s (max line-of-sight rate the seeker tracks); fov = the seeker block's field of view, degrees (null when the missile has no such block); dMin / dMax = D_min / D_max, m (launch ranges); rangeMax = Range_max, m; fuze = KillDistance, m (the proximity-fuze radius when the missile has a proximity-fuze block); life = Life_Time, s; power = seeker power time, s (ModelData[36], 1-based); src = the file:line of the seeker sensitivity. Missiles with a sensor, IR_seeker or simple_IR_seeker block (P_27T, P_27TE, RIM_116A, FIM_92C, OH58D_FIM_92, CHAP_AIM92, Igla_1E, Mistral, MIM_72G) take ssd, ccm, fov and power from that block (sensitivity, ccm_k0, FOV, opTime), gimbal and trackRate from their gimbal block (az_max, max_tracking_rate) or simple_gyrostab_seeker (gimbal_lim, omega_max). null = DCS gives no value or its 99.9 'no limit' placeholder. missileAliases: normalised name (strip 'weapons.missiles.' / 'weapons.nurs.', lowercase, keep a-z0-9) -> DCS missile name, from every rocket's name, display_name and user_name plus common short names; names that fit two missiles are left out; an exact DCS name always wins. guidance: every other DCS missile -> its Head_Type (2 active radar, 3 anti-radiation, 4 laser, 5 autonomous/INS/TV/IIR, 6 semi-active radar, 7 command/ATGM, 8 undocumented: command SAMs), so a name can be known not to be IR. DCS does not publish how these combine into a lock range; any range the app shows is an estimate.","aspect":{"front":0.5,"beam":1.0,"rear":1.5,"src":"_G/prbCoeff.lua:19 (k7 = 0.5: front k7, side 1, rear 2 - k7)"},"fov":2.0,"planes":{"A-10A":[0.53,null],"A-10C":[0.53,null],"A-10C_2":[0.53,null],"A-20G":[0.1,null],"A-50":[4,null],"A6E":[0.62,0.62],"AH-1W":[0.2,null],"AH-64A":[0.2,null],"AH-64D":[0.2,null],"AH-64D_BLK_II":[0.2,null],"AJS37":[0.62,2],"AV8BNA":[0.7,null],"An-26B":[0.5,null],"An-30M":[0.5,null],"B-17G":[0.1,null],"B-1B":[3,8],"B-52H":[4,null],"Bf-109K-4":[0.1,null],"C-101CC":[0.2,null],"C-101EB":[0.2,null],"C-130":[1,null],"C-130J-30":[1,null],"C-17A":[3,null],"C-47":[0.1,null],"CH-47D":[0.72,null],"CH-47Fbl1":[0.1,null],"CH-53E":[1,null],"CHAP_TigerUHT":[0.25,null],"Christen Eagle II":[0.04,null],"E-2C":[0.5,null],"E-3A":[4,null],"F-100D":[0.8,2.6],"F-117A":[0.15,null],"F-14A":[0.97,5],"F-14A-135-GR":[0.9,4.75],"F-14A-135-GR-Early":[0.9,4.75],"F-14A-95-GR":[0.9,4.75],"F-14B":[0.9,4.75],"F-14BU":[0.9,4.75],"F-15C":[0.85,4.25],"F-15E":[0.91,4],"F-15ESE":[0.91,4],"F-16A":[0.6,3],"F-16A MLU":[0.6,3],"F-16C bl.50":[0.6,3],"F-16C bl.52d":[0.6,3],"F-16C_50":[0.6,3],"F-4E":[1,4],"F-4E-45MC":[0.8,4],"F-5E":[0.4,2],"F-5E-3":[0.4,2],"F-5E-3_